pkg/proc, service/debugger, pkg/terminal: restart to a point where its goroutine yields stays there

restart sN, kN or tD ran to runtime.detDebugStop and then continued to
the return of runtime.detPreempt in the stopped goroutine, to leave the
runtime for the goroutine's code. When the point is the last tick of
the goroutine's quantum, detPreempt yields after the stop, as the run
does without it, so the goroutine came back there only after other
goroutines ran: the stop reported a later switch (and often a later
tick) than GODETSTOP's stop line for the same point.

The runtime now says at each stop whether the goroutine yields there,
in runtime.detDebug.yields. restart then stays at runtime.detDebugStop,
at the point's exact position, and says which frame is the goroutine's
code:

	goroutine 158 yields here, at the last tick of its quantum, so its code goes on only at a later switch; frame 3 is its code: net.(*netFD).connect.func2() .../src/net/fd_unix.go:94

A runtime without the field keeps the old behavior.


